          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "{\n \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\",\n \"name\": \"Forensics.lean\",\n \"url\": \"https://uuidna.com/lean/Forensics.lean\",\n \"inLanguage\": \"lean4\",\n \"variableMeasured\": {\n  \"@type\": \"PropertyValue\",\n  \"name\": \"theorems\",\n  \"value\": 3,\n  \"unitText\": \"theorem\"\n }\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-forged_address_odds_are_negligible",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A GUESSED ADDRESS DOES NOT LAND. The ledger holds 71,085 distinct addresses, every one a v8 uuid with 122 free bits, so a forger who invents an address and frames it as sealed hits a real one with odds below 2^-105: 71,085 × 2^105 < 2^122. forensics() flags every miss as a false address — run here on a forged address (flagged) and a sealed one (passed) — so a false trial cannot survive except by that chance, and the chance is sealed. Counted from the ledger at generation, never typed."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "71085 * 2 ^ 105 < 2 ^ 122"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem forged_address_odds_are_negligible : 71085 * 2 ^ 105 < 2 ^ 122 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-forged_handle_odds_are_small",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A GUESSED HANDLE RARELY LANDS EITHER. The handle store holds 71,705 leaves in a 32-bit handle space, so a guessed handle names an occupied leaf with odds below 2^-15: 71,705 × 2^15 < 2^32. The odds are far weaker than an address's, which is why a handle is only ever the PATH to a leaf and the leaf itself carries the full uuid that forensics() checks."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "71705 * 2 ^ 15 < 2 ^ 32"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem forged_handle_odds_are_small : 71705 * 2 ^ 15 < 2 ^ 32 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-sixteen_bit_handles_would_collide",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "THE CONTROL: THE BOUND CAN FAIL. With 16-bit handles the store's 71,705 leaves would outnumber the 65,536 handles available, so two leaves would be forced to share one — pigeonhole, not chance — and the store refuses any collision. The odds above are a property of the widths chosen, and a width too small is refuted by the same arithmetic; that is why a handle carries 32 bits."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "71705 > 2 ^ 16"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem sixteen_bit_handles_would_collide : 71705 > 2 ^ 16 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
